>   What do you do with sinks!! I can make the pipes vibrate ok and have
>snakes come pouring out, but thats it. What purpose do they serve??
Snakes?  Yum!  Other things will come out, too.  As in many other
places in this games, persistence favors.  But be prepared for the
unpleasant!
>  Also, I have offered lots of stuff to the alter, I assume its my altar
>because it says that it is an aligned one I belive. I offer up some dead
>creature and it is consumed in flames then I get the message:
>"There is a conflict between Thor and Ptah,unluckily for you Thor
>decreases" or something similar. Whats happening.
You're sacrificing at an altar of some other god than the one with which
you started.  Remember that you *can* change your alignment as the game
goes on.  Also you can, as they say, alter the alter.
> From what I have read
>I thought if I put a scroll on the altar it would become a blessed
>scroll, so far this had not happened.
True, it won't happen often.  Ever, in fact.  Keep dropping stuff on
the altar.  At least one thing in the game will be transformed (you
could guess which one if you thought about it).
>
>  Thanks for the help. Maybe with some good advice and hints I might
>make it past level 5. Oh ya, I forgot. I currently am playing a Wizard,
>not sure if that makes a difference.
It does.  I found wizards hard at first, now they're among the easiest to
finish.  Barbarians are easier to keep alive until you figure stuff out,
as are priests (because you know what's blessed).  Wizards are hard to
keep alive unless you're willing to run away a lot at the beginning.
The best advice is to try everything you can think of.  Many, many things
have more than one function, and some things you do by accident will
amuse you greatly.  Have fun!

